DAY_DATA = {'day': 156, 'part1_intro': "Day 156 — Cymbal Retail — catalog and commerce requirements — uses the roadmap's case or exam scope as the input. Each topic names the decision boundary, evidence owner and business effect; no product choice or score is treated as a fact without supporting evidence.", 'part2_intro': 'Trace the full reasoning path: supplied fact or requirement, candidate design or study rule, acceptance evidence, failure signal, owner and condition that would change the choice. The topology is a teaching model, not evidence of a live system or exam result.', 'part3_intro': 'These deep-dive cases preserve the original case or exam reasoning while separating supplied facts from architectural inference. The incident diagrams are synthetic exercises, not observed production events.', 'part4_intro': "The labs retain each day's original decision work, expanded into the eight execution stages used on Day 142. Complete them with prior artifacts and synthetic inputs unless an earlier roadmap page explicitly authorizes a cloud test.", 'exit_summary': 'A fact register and content approval/data-flow diagram with security boundaries.', 'arch_table_html': '\n<table><caption>Day-specific architecture and evidence path</caption><thead><tr><th>Topic boundary</th><th>Decision rule</th><th>Acceptance evidence</th><th>Limit</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>Read the official Cymbal Retail case</td><td>Separate supplied fact, requirement and proposed control.</td><td>One artifact, one rejected alternative and one changed-constraint result.</td><td>Local/tabletop evidence cannot prove production behavior or exam performance.</td></tr><tr><td>Capture supplier integration, generated content, discovery and human review</td><td>Separate supplied fact, requirement and proposed control.</td><td>One artifact, one rejected alternative and one changed-constraint result.</td><td>Local/tabletop evidence cannot prove production behavior or exam performance.</td></tr></tbody></table>', 'arch_diagram': {'type': 'topology', 'title': 'Day 156: Cymbal Retail — catalog and commerce requirements — evidence and decision path', 'desc': 'Three-tier architecture path for Cymbal Retail — catalog and commerce requirements, showing case or exam inputs, requirements and trade-off evidence, then acceptance and ownership controls.', 'caption': 'Scope: a synthetic evidence path for Day 156 covering Read the official Cymbal Retail case / Capture supplier integration, generated co. It shows reasoning boundaries and verification ownership; it does not prove a production deployment, exam result, price, quota, eligibility or customer outcome.', 'width': 1120, 'height': 690, 'layers': [{'name': 'TIER 1 · INPUTS / DEMAND', 'desc': 'case facts, prompts and constraints', 'x': 10, 'y': 55, 'w': 1100, 'h': 92, 'fill': '#0c2033', 'title_color': '#38bdf8', 'opacity': 0.72}, {'name': 'TIER 2 · EVIDENCE / REASONING', 'desc': 'requirements, alternatives and failure checks', 'x': 10, 'y': 185, 'w': 1100, 'h': 210, 'fill': '#241808', 'title_color': '#f59e0b', 'opacity': 0.64}, {'name': 'TIER 3 · GOVERNANCE / ACCEPTANCE', 'desc': 'owners, acceptance and revisit triggers', 'x': 10, 'y': 435, 'w': 1100, 'h': 115, 'fill': '#062316', 'title_color': '#22c55e', 'opacity': 0.68}], 'components': [{'name': 'Case or prompt', 'detail': 'Day 156 supplied scope', 'x': 60, 'y': 78, 'w': 250, 'h': 56, 'stroke': '#38bdf8', 'fill': '#102a42'}, {'name': 'Prior artifacts', 'detail': 'facts + decisions + errors', 'x': 435, 'y': 78, 'w': 250, 'h': 56, 'stroke': '#38bdf8', 'fill': '#102a42'}, {'name': 'Changed constraint', 'detail': 'cost / risk / scope', 'x': 810, 'y': 78, 'w': 250, 'h': 56, 'stroke': '#38bdf8', 'fill': '#102a42'}, {'name': 'Requirements map', 'detail': 'fact to acceptance', 'x': 60, 'y': 220, 'w': 250, 'h': 105, 'stroke': '#f59e0b', 'fill': '#3b2508'}, {'name': 'Option matrix', 'detail': 'choice + alternative', 'x': 435, 'y': 220, 'w': 250, 'h': 105, 'stroke': '#f59e0b', 'fill': '#3b2508'}, {'name': 'Failure rehearsal', 'detail': 'signal + safe response', 'x': 810, 'y': 220, 'w': 250, 'h': 105, 'stroke': '#f59e0b', 'fill': '#3b2508'}, {'name': 'Evidence owner', 'detail': 'source + artifact', 'x': 245, 'y': 455, 'w': 250, 'h': 70, 'stroke': '#22c55e', 'fill': '#064e3b'}, {'name': 'Acceptance gate', 'detail': 'observed / predicted', 'x': 625, 'y': 455, 'w': 250, 'h': 70, 'stroke': '#22c55e', 'fill': '#064e3b'}], 'flows': [{'x1': 185, 'y1': 134, 'x2': 185, 'y2': 220, 'type': 'ok', 'label': 'extract'}, {'x1': 560, 'y1': 134, 'x2': 560, 'y2': 220, 'type': 'ok', 'label': 'trace'}, {'x1': 935, 'y1': 134, 'x2': 935, 'y2': 220, 'type': 'warn', 'label': 'challenge'}, {'x1': 310, 'y1': 272, 'x2': 435, 'y2': 272, 'type': 'ok', 'label': 'compare'}, {'x1': 685, 'y1': 272, 'x2': 810, 'y2': 272, 'type': 'ok', 'label': 'rehearse'}, {'x1': 935, 'y1': 325, 'x2': 750, 'y2': 455, 'type': 'ok', 'label': 'accept'}, {'x1': 560, 'y1': 325, 'x2': 370, 'y2': 455, 'type': 'warn', 'label': 'evidence'}, {'x1': 495, 'y1': 490, 'x2': 625, 'y2': 490, 'type': 'ok', 'label': 'review'}], 'boundaries': [{'x': 42, 'y': 205, 'w': 1036, 'h': 140, 'color': '#f59e0b', 'label': 'EVIDENCE CHECK'}, {'x': 220, 'y': 442, 'w': 680, 'h': 94, 'color': '#22c55e', 'label': 'DECISION OWNER'}], 'probes': [{'cx': 185, 'cy': 106, 'label': 'PROBE 1 · input classified', 'badge': 'P1', 'color': '#38bdf8'}, {'cx': 560, 'cy': 272, 'label': 'PROBE 2 · trade-off recorded', 'badge': 'P2', 'color': '#f59e0b'}, {'cx': 750, 'cy': 490, 'label': 'PROBE 3 · acceptance result', 'badge': 'P3', 'color': '#22c55e'}]}, 'topics': [{'key': 'topic-01', 'title': 'Read the official Cymbal Retail case', 'overview': 'Cymbal is an online retailer with a large catalog. The official case describes catalog enrichment, conversational commerce and technical-stack modernization over an environment that mixes on-premises and cloud systems, several databases, Kubernetes, file/SFTP and ETL integrations, an existing web application, IVR/call-center workflows and open-source monitoring.', 'preview': 'Symptom: A generated description overwrites a supplier attribute, while a later supplier correction is treated as a duplicate and discarded. Effect: The read the official cymbal retail case decision remains unverified.', 'technical': '<p>Start with the existing environment, not the desired product. Record the current source for supplier attributes, catalog identity, price/inventory, customer interactions and order entry. Then separate the business outcomes—less manual effort, better discovery, engagement, conversion and lower cost—from technical requirements such as attribute generation, image variation, scale, HITL review, security and compliance.</p><table><caption>Cymbal fact-to-requirement register</caption><thead><tr><th>Supplied case fact</th><th>Requirement</th><th>Boundary to clarify</th><th>Acceptance evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Supplier data arrives through existing integrations</td><td>Enrich products without losing source authority.</td><td>Identity, schema/version, duplicate and correction handling.</td><td>Reconciled fixture with source and derived fields.</td></tr><tr><td>Several databases and Kubernetes workloads exist</td><td>Modernize without breaking order/catalog dependencies.</td><td>Read/write ownership, compatibility and migration sequence.</td><td>Dependency map and rollback fixture.</td></tr><tr><td>Conversational discovery is desired</td><td>Return relevant products for natural-language requests.</td><td>Inventory freshness, ranking, personalization and access.</td><td>Relevance and authorization test set.</td></tr><tr><td>Associates must approve generated content</td><td>Provide review, edit, approve and reject states before publication.</td><td>Workflow identity, audit and conflict resolution.</td><td>State transition log and rejected-content test.</td></tr></tbody></table><p><a href="../sources.html#topic-048">Topic 048 source section</a>; current publisher material was checked 2026-09-30. Separate supplied facts, local observations and proposed controls.</p>', 'questions': ['Which requirement bounds the selected option?', 'What observable evidence supports the decision?', 'Which changed constraint would reverse the choice?', 'Who owns the failure response and review?'], 'reference': 'https://services.google.com/fh/files/misc/v6.1_pca_cymbal_retail_case_study_english.pdf', 'reference_label': 'Official Topic 48 source (checked 2026-09-30)', 'scenario': {'scenario': 'A generated description overwrites a supplier attribute, while a later supplier correction is treated as a duplicate and discarded. Sales channels diverge and a call-center agent sees different information from the website.', 'impact': '', 'constraints': 'Use synthetic data, preserve the prior artifact and keep unknown behavior explicitly labeled.', 'facts': 'The case statement and artifact are teaching inputs; no production incident or learner result is claimed.', 'inference': 'The design lacked stable product/version identities and separated neither source fields nor derived fields. Retain provenance, version updates, define conflict ownership and publish only approved catalog states. Reconcile every channel against the approved version.', 'root': 'The design lacked stable product/version identities and separated neither source fields nor derived fields. Retain provenance, version updates, define conflict ownership and publish only approved catalog states. Reconcile every channel against the approved version.', 'fix': 'The design lacked stable product/version identities and separated neither source fields nor derived fields. Retain provenance, version updates, define conflict ownership and publish only approved catalog states. Reconcile every channel against the approved version.', 'verify': 'Re-run the bounded case, compare it with the declared acceptance signal and save the resulting decision trace.', 'residual': 'Synthetic rows cannot prove supplier quality or production-scale throughput. Record the data owner and the test needed before rollout.', 'diagram': ('supplied trigger', 'missing or untested control', 'business and operating impact', 'bounded defensive control', 'verified evidence artifact')}, 'lab': {'name': 'Extract Cymbal facts and boundaries', 'goal': 'Create a source-linked fact register and existing-versus-proposed catalog/data-flow diagram.', 'expected': 'A source-linked matrix and diagram that distinguish existing systems, proposed AI, approval boundaries and open questions.', 'mode': 'local/tabletop with synthetic data; no cloud access or spend', 'prereq': 'Bring the prior case or exam artifact and record it unavailable if missing.', 'preflight': 'Use `day-156-01-extract-cymbal-facts-and-boundaries.md`; record the source, access date, prior artifact, owner and synthetic-data boundary.', 'steps': ['**Stage 1 — Preflight and validate assumptions/environment.** Create `day-156-01-extract-cymbal-facts-and-boundaries.md`. Record Day 156, the prior artifact, the source `https://services.google.com/fh/files/misc/v6.1_pca_cymbal_retail_case_study_english.pdf`, the access date, a named owner and the statement that the exercise uses synthetic or tabletop evidence only.', '**Stage 2 — Prepare the target, inputs, or backing resources.** Open the source. Create day-156-cymbal-facts.md ; record the official PDF URL and page for each claim.', '**Stage 3 — Author the plan, configuration, or analysis.** Register facts. Capture systems, databases, integrations, actors, business outcomes and technical requirements.', '**Stage 4 — Execute or simulate the planned change.** Mark ownership. For product identity, supplier input, generated field, approval state, price, inventory and customer interaction, name the source of truth.', '**Stage 5 — Inspect expected state and verify outcomes.** Draw the flow. Show supplier/SFTP or ETL, staging, enrichment, review, publication, search/discovery and order/call-center paths.', '**Stage 6 — Rehearse a bounded failure, edge case, or decision challenge.** Inject an error. Change one supplier attribute, send a duplicate file or reject an image. Record the first changed state and correction path.', '**Stage 7 — Diagnose evidence and record remediation/decision.** Save. Link the fact register and diagram from the daily artifact.', '**Stage 8 — Clean up or close out the exercise.** Save `day-156-01-extract-cymbal-facts-and-boundaries.md`, link it from the daily artifact, keep the evidence, remove only disposable copies and state what needs an authorized or production verification.'], 'verification': 'A source-linked matrix and diagram that distinguish existing systems, proposed AI, approval boundaries and open questions.', 'accept': 'The saved artifact identifies the requirement, selected and rejected options, acceptance evidence, failure response, owner and residual risk.', 'trouble': 'If a technology appears in the case, do not assume it is the correct replacement; record its current role and the decision still required.', 'cleanup': 'Keep the evidence artifact and remove only disposable copies. No cloud resource, credential, payment detail or protected exam content belongs in this exercise.', 'file': 'day-156-01-extract-cymbal-facts-and-boundaries.md'}}, {'key': 'topic-02', 'title': 'Capture supplier integration, generated content, discovery and human review', 'overview': 'Generated attributes, descriptions and images are derived content. They must be validated against category schema, supplier evidence and the approval policy before they update the catalog. Conversational discovery must retrieve from approved product data and must not invent availability, price or product claims.', 'preview': 'Symptom: A customer asks for a product with a particular feature. Effect: The capture supplier integration, generated content, discovery and human review decision remains unverified.', 'technical': '<p>Use a content state machine such as <code>received → normalized → generated → validated → needs-review → approved/rejected → published</code>. Keep source and derived values separate, attach a product and content version, and make reprocessing idempotent. The review UI needs role separation, diff visibility, rejection reasons and an audit record.</p><p>For discovery, define the query contract, retrieval corpus, ranking signal, inventory/price freshness and safe fallback. A conversational agent can help a user find products, but order creation and inventory claims need authoritative systems and explicit authorization. Image generation needs content-policy, brand and product-identity checks. Measure relevance and business outcomes separately from model fluency.</p><div class="callout"><strong>Acceptance rule</strong><p>No generated field reaches a customer-facing channel without a valid product identity, schema validation, provenance, policy decision and a reversible publication record.</p></div><p><a href="../sources.html#topic-048">Topic 048 source section</a>; current publisher material was checked 2026-09-30. Separate supplied facts, local observations and proposed controls.</p>', 'questions': ['Which requirement bounds the selected option?', 'What observable evidence supports the decision?', 'Which changed constraint would reverse the choice?', 'Who owns the failure response and review?'], 'reference': 'https://services.google.com/fh/files/misc/v6.1_pca_cymbal_retail_case_study_english.pdf', 'reference_label': 'Official Topic 48 source (checked 2026-09-30)', 'scenario': {'scenario': 'A customer asks for a product with a particular feature. Retrieval finds a similar item, but the assistant claims the item is in stock and suitable. The response came from stale catalog text rather than the inventory or product-attribute authority.', 'impact': '', 'constraints': 'Use synthetic data, preserve the prior artifact and keep unknown behavior explicitly labeled.', 'facts': 'The case statement and artifact are teaching inputs; no production incident or learner result is claimed.', 'inference': 'Discovery, recommendation, inventory and order authority were conflated. Restrict retrieval to approved content, call authoritative inventory only when needed, show a safe uncertainty response and log the evidence used. Add adversarial and stale-data tests.', 'root': 'Discovery, recommendation, inventory and order authority were conflated. Restrict retrieval to approved content, call authoritative inventory only when needed, show a safe uncertainty response and log the evidence used. Add adversarial and stale-data tests.', 'fix': 'Discovery, recommendation, inventory and order authority were conflated. Restrict retrieval to approved content, call authoritative inventory only when needed, show a safe uncertainty response and log the evidence used. Add adversarial and stale-data tests.', 'verify': 'Re-run the bounded case, compare it with the declared acceptance signal and save the resulting decision trace.', 'residual': 'A relevance score is not a guarantee of factual correctness or conversion. Maintain human review for sensitive categories and measure returns, complaints and correction time.', 'diagram': ('supplied trigger', 'missing or untested control', 'business and operating impact', 'bounded defensive control', 'verified evidence artifact')}, 'lab': {'name': 'Design the content approval and discovery contract', 'goal': 'Create a synthetic approval workflow and a conversational-discovery acceptance checklist.', 'expected': 'A reversible content workflow and discovery contract with source authority, HITL review, authorization and safe failure.', 'mode': 'local/tabletop with synthetic data; no cloud access or spend', 'prereq': 'Bring the prior case or exam artifact and record it unavailable if missing.', 'preflight': 'Use `day-156-02-design-the-content-approval-and-disc.md`; record the source, access date, prior artifact, owner and synthetic-data boundary.', 'steps': ['**Stage 1 — Preflight and validate assumptions/environment.** Create `day-156-02-design-the-content-approval-and-disc.md`. Record Day 156, the prior artifact, the source `https://services.google.com/fh/files/misc/v6.1_pca_cymbal_retail_case_study_english.pdf`, the access date, a named owner and the statement that the exercise uses synthetic or tabletop evidence only.', '**Stage 2 — Prepare the target, inputs, or backing resources.** Create fixtures. Use synthetic supplier rows, one duplicate, one malformed attribute, one generated image and one stale inventory row.', '**Stage 3 — Author the plan, configuration, or analysis.** Define schema. Write product ID, source version, derived value, confidence, reviewer, state, rejection reason and publication timestamp.', '**Stage 4 — Execute or simulate the planned change.** Run transitions. Move each fixture through normalization, generation, validation, review and approval/rejection. Preserve the audit trail.', '**Stage 5 — Inspect expected state and verify outcomes.** Test discovery. Ask a natural-language query that requires category, attribute and inventory. Mark what may be answered and what must come from an authority.', '**Stage 6 — Rehearse a bounded failure, edge case, or decision challenge.** Inject failure. Remove the inventory response or feed a conflicting supplier update. Record the safe response and reconciliation action.', '**Stage 7 — Diagnose evidence and record remediation/decision.** Accept. Save the state machine, test results and remaining owner questions.', '**Stage 8 — Clean up or close out the exercise.** Save `day-156-02-design-the-content-approval-and-disc.md`, link it from the daily artifact, keep the evidence, remove only disposable copies and state what needs an authorized or production verification.'], 'verification': 'A reversible content workflow and discovery contract with source authority, HITL review, authorization and safe failure.', 'accept': 'The saved artifact identifies the requirement, selected and rejected options, acceptance evidence, failure response, owner and residual risk.', 'trouble': 'If the generated answer sounds plausible but has no source or current inventory evidence, classify it as unsafe draft output.', 'cleanup': 'Keep the evidence artifact and remove only disposable copies. No cloud resource, credential, payment detail or protected exam content belongs in this exercise.', 'file': 'day-156-02-design-the-content-approval-and-disc.md'}}]}
